'''Kunio-kun''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by purchasing the 11-draw Capsule at the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[River City Ransom Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.9 Update|Version 10.9]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 624
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Kunio-kun
|name2 = Dodgeball Kunio-kun
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dodgeball Kunio-kun''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
The most unique feature about this unit is his single-slot [[Cat Combo|combo]] which increases [[Worker Cat]]'s starting level by 2. This is an extremely efficient combo for the amount of space it takes, even beating [[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)|Richest Cat]] (+500 starting funds and +1 Worker starting level) when it comes to monetary advantage on cash-tight stages, and arguably the biggest benefit that having this unit will provide. It can also be further augmented with other combos to grant your worker a huge starting level boost, such as [[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Riches]], [[Cat Transport (Combo)|Cat Transport]] and [[Longnecks (Combo)|Longnecks]]. Aside from that, this unit, although not that powerful when it comes to stats in either form, can be switched between completely different forms, offering the player two different options for what to do with him.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Kunio-kun is a melee attacker similar to [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], with both decent health and damage. His multi-hit makes him ideal not only for damage, but also to tank while shaking off peons often, though not too efficiently, seeing the very short interval between the multiple hits.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Dodgeball Kunio-Kun changes his usage completely, basically becoming a different unit. His now impressive range is his new main feature, which allows him to snipe enemies from a safe distance, switching from protecting others to being the one in need of protection. If that is granted, however, he will last a long time, doing damage from the back. His speed will lead him into danger though, so avoid using the [[Cat Cannon]] while he is idle, as he might sprint too far forwards for his own good. Although his damage isn't great and his health is very low in this form, he makes up for it with an impressively low cost for such stats, allowing him to often be a good investment.

